<main id="main">

<section class="an-hero"><div class="an-w an-hero-g"><div class="an-hero-t"><p class="an-mono">// field guide &middot; vol. 01</p><h1>Pull it on.<br><span>Face the</span><br>weather.</h1><p class="an-lead">Anoraky is an independent field guide to the anorak, the pullover shell that has kept people out of wind and rain for centuries. Work out what to wear under it, how much it needs to breathe and why the hood is the best part.</p>
<div class="an-hero-a"><a class="an-btn" href="#wind">Check wind chill</a><a class="an-btn an-btn-o" href="#vent">Match breathability</a></div><dl class="an-hud"><div><dt>Wind</dt><dd><b data-count="35">0</b> km/h</dd></div><div><dt>Temp</dt><dd><b data-count="4">0</b> &deg;C</dd></div><div><dt>Feels</dt><dd><b>&minus;2</b> &deg;C</dd></div></dl></div>
<div class="an-hero-v"><figure class="an-hi1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1789243596951-cd191a456821?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=700&q=75" alt="a person in a blue rain jacket and backpack walking" width="560" height="700" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="an-hi2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788035839400-ec06b90edbb1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=360&q=75" alt="a man in an orange and blue hooded jacket" width="300" height="360" fetchpriority="high"></figure><svg class="an-wind" viewBox="0 0 300 120" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 30h180c30 0 30-26 8-26"/><path d="M10 60h240c30 0 30 30 6 30"/><path d="M10 90h120"/></svg></div></div></section>

<section class="an-s an-wc" id="wind"><div class="an-w an-wc-g"><div><p class="an-mono">[ tool 01 ]</p><h2 class="rv">Wind chill &amp; layer planner</h2><p class="an-p">Wind steals heat, which is exactly what an anorak is built to stop. Enter the air temperature and wind speed to see what it feels like, and what to wear underneath your shell.</p>
<div class="an-units" role="group" aria-label="Units"><button type="button" class="on" data-u="c">&deg;C &middot; km/h</button><button type="button" data-u="f">&deg;F &middot; mph</button></div>
<label class="an-lb" for="wc-t">Air temperature <b id="wc-tv"></b></label><input type="range" id="wc-t" min="-30" max="15" value="4" class="an-rng">
<label class="an-lb" for="wc-w">Wind speed <b id="wc-wv"></b></label><input type="range" id="wc-w" min="0" max="80" value="35" class="an-rng"><figure class="an-wc-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1761774958425-cb1e7a5439e2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=240&q=75" alt="a person with arms outstretched on a windy hilltop" width="560" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="an-panel" aria-live="polite"><div class="an-feel"><span class="an-mono">feels like</span><b id="wc-f"></b><i id="wc-r"></i></div><div class="an-stack" id="wc-s"></div><p class="an-note" id="wc-n"></p></div></div></section>

<section class="an-s an-vt" id="vent"><div class="an-w an-vt-g"><div class="an-panel an-vt-p" aria-live="polite"><div class="an-dial"><svg viewBox="0 0 240 140" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 120a100 100 0 0 1 200 0" class="d0"/><path d="M20 120a100 100 0 0 1 200 0" class="d1" id="vt-arc"/><g id="vt-n" class="nd"><path d="M120 120L120 34"/><circle cx="120" cy="120" r="8"/></g></svg><b id="vt-v"></b><span class="an-mono">breathability needed</span></div><ul class="an-tips" id="vt-l"></ul></div>
<div><p class="an-mono">[ tool 02 ]</p><h2 class="rv">Breathability matcher</h2><p class="an-p">A shell that keeps rain out can also keep sweat in. Tell us how hard you will work and what the air is like, and we suggest how breathable your anorak should be and how to vent it.</p>
<p class="an-lb">Effort</p><div class="an-seg" id="vt-e"><button type="button" data-v="0">Stroll</button><button type="button" class="on" data-v="1">Brisk walk</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Hike uphill</button><button type="button" data-v="3">Run or ride</button></div>
<p class="an-lb">Air</p><div class="an-seg" id="vt-h"><button type="button" data-v="0">Dry &amp; cold</button><button type="button" class="on" data-v="1">Damp &amp; mild</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Warm &amp; muggy</button></div>
<p class="an-lb">Rain</p><div class="an-seg" id="vt-r"><button type="button" data-v="0">None</button><button type="button" class="on" data-v="1">Showers</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Steady</button></div><figure class="an-vt-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1603741614725-2fbf5db380e1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=240&q=75" alt="a man in an orange hoodie on a rocky mountain" width="560" height="240" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="an-s an-dts"><div class="an-w"><div class="an-dts-h"><p class="an-mono">[ anatomy ]</p><h2 class="rv">Three details that make an anorak</h2></div><div class="an-dts-g"><article class="an-dt rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1668954443591-ea2072a6b4b0?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a close-up of a zipper" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="an-mono">01</span><b>Half-zip front</b><p>Pulls on over the head and vents fast with one tug.</p></article><article class="an-dt rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1745265798290-d1f238b29a9d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="water droplets on blue fabric" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="an-mono">02</span><b>Shed-it shell</b><p>A tight weave or membrane that beads water away.</p></article><article class="an-dt rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1715606490545-59eb9c54251d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a mannequin wearing a blue hooded jacket" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="an-mono">03</span><b>Storm hood</b><p>Wraps the face and turns with your head.</p></article></div><div class="an-wide"><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1689835776638-456cc2503de4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=400&q=75" alt="a person in a red jacket looking at a lighthouse" width="620" height="400" loading="lazy"></figure><figure class="rv"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1782174358357-b7338e3f1437?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=400&q=75" alt="a person in a hooded raincoat walking in the rain" width="460" height="400" loading="lazy"></figure><p class="an-wide-t rv">Coastal paths, city drizzle, wild headlands: one pullover shell covers them all.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="an-gd"><div class="an-w an-gd-g"><a class="an-gc rv" href="anorak-history-guide.html"><span class="an-mono">guide / 01</span><b>The Anorak Story</b><p>From Arctic skin parkas to the half-zip shell on every high street.</p><em>Read &rarr;</em></a><a class="an-gc an-gc2 rv" href="layering-under-a-shell-guide.html"><span class="an-mono">guide / 02</span><b>Layering Under a Shell</b><p>Base, mid and outer: how to stay warm, dry and comfortable all day.</p><em>Read &rarr;</em></a></div></section>

